Thanks for getting back to me and good to know your preferences on remote
vs. hybrid. I'll keep that in mind as I evaluate opportunities that fit
your criteria.

Just to make sure I'm being completely transparent  I'm a Reverse
Recruiter, which means I work for you, not for the hiring company. Unlike
traditional recruiters who are paid by employers to fill roles, I partner
directly with job seekers to help them navigate the job market more
strategically and land roles that align with their goals.

Here's what that looks like in practice:

=C2=B7 Opportunity identification  I actively surface strong-fit, high-quality
roles that match your experience, compensation targets, and location
preferences (like the remote/hybrid flexibility you mentioned).
=C2=B7 Direct connection strategy Instead of relying only on online
applications, I help you get in front of hiring managers and recruiters
through targeted outreach and relationship building.
=C2=B7 Positioning & application support I help refine your narrative, tailor
your materials, and provide tools to strengthen your visibility and
competitiveness throughout the hiring process.
=C2=B7 Ongoing strategic guidance  From interview prep to offer negotiation, I
support you at every stage to make sure you're putting your best foot
forward.

The opportunity I mentioned is a real one, but more importantly, my goal is
to help you find the right opportunity whether that's this one or another
that fits your criteria. The value I add is helping you move through the
job search more efficiently and with greater visibility than going it alone.

Would you be open to continuing the conversation? If so, I'd love to learn
a bit more about what you're looking for in your next role and share how I
can support you in landing it.

Looking forward to hearing from you.

Best Regards,
*MASHOOD SEKINAT *
*REVERSE RECRUITER | EXECUTIVE JOB SEARCH STRATEGIST | EXECUTIVE BRANDING
SPEALCIALIST*



